  "Number": 3,
  "Question": "For \\(x\\ne0,\\) \\(\\frac1x+\\frac1{2x}+\\frac1{3x}\\) equals",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\frac1{2x}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\frac1{6x}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\frac5{6x}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\frac{11}{6x}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\frac1{6x^3}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "To add the fractions, give them the common denominator \\(6x\\), which is nonzero because \\(x\\ne0\\). Then\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac1x+\\frac1{2x}+\\frac1{3x}\n&=\\frac6{6x}+\\frac3{6x}+\\frac2{6x}\\\\\n&=\\frac{6+3+2}{6x}\\\\\n&=\\frac{11}{6x}.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\frac{11}{6x}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
